      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for looking into this Jie Chen. I do think it\u0027s a bug that `$blend_porter_duff` is universally applying the `min(1` to its calculations. However, we can\u0027t remove the `min` for the plus blend mode as that is documented behavior.\n\nPlus is in an awkward spot where it\u0027s math is the only one that can produce values outside of its gamut. When colors were always normalized to [0,1] adding the min made sense. When doing plus blending on hdr content, you have to clamp the alpha channel but what do you clamp the other channels too? We\u0027ve historically continued to just clamp it to 1.\n\nIt\u0027s unlikely that chrome is using the plus blend mode for the issues in the linked bug, though. This function is also used in Ganesh as well, so it\u0027s unclear to me how Graphite is triggering this blend when Ganesh is using something else (both should be able to convert plus into hardware blending if it\u0027s the final blend mode). Were you able to export the shaders that were proving problematic?",
